-- METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000033 and 2192 as the visible case of its family).
-- WHAT WAS FOUND (read 2026-10-26 from live qnfo-audit, read-only): metrics_on_probation_overdue (target 0) counts metric_authorship rows that are still on probation after probation_until (the trigger
--   kernel_registries_tick on fleet_tick, migrations/2026-10-12-20-kernel-registries.sql). A metric that cannot produce a value until a sample floor is met can never graduate, so the counter can never stay at 0 for it:
--   ask_helpful_rate_30d (formula "... unmeasured below 10 ratings") and q08_forecast_void_share ("... written once at least 10 forecasts are finished") were both counted. It reads 0 today only because
--   migrations/2026-10-19-impact-per-dollar-zenodo-null.sql extended both probation dates by hand to 2026-11-18T08:02:17Z (a recorded decision, not a fix): on 2026-11-18 the counter reads 2 again.
--   The issue proposes to treat a NULL value below an explicit sample floor as "awaiting samples", counted apart, and keep counting a metric with no sample gate and no value; it forbids marking the rows dormant,
--   closing them as wontfix, or hiding the fact that they cannot measure yet. The counter itself lives in a fleet_tick trigger that this file does not recreate (the 2026-10-26 04:42Z SQLITE_NOMEM outage came from a
--   fleet_tick trigger), so the rule is applied to the data the counter reads.
-- WHAT THIS FILE DOES:
--   1. fleet_tasks metric-refresh gets two steps (appended with json_insert at steps[#], the pattern of migrations/2026-10-02-act-bridge-doer-metrics.sql; the executor stops a workflow at its first failing step, and
--      these are last): probation-sample-gate moves probation_until 30 days ahead for a probation metric that is within 2 days of it (or past it), has no value, and whose formula carries a minimum-sample clause
--      ("unmeasured below", "written once at least" or "minimum sample"); a metric with no sample gate and no value is left alone and still counts as overdue. awaiting-samples writes the new metric
--      metrics_awaiting_samples: the probation metrics with no value and a sample gate (2 on 2026-10-26), so what cannot measure yet stays visible, apart from the overdue count.
--   2. metrics_awaiting_samples is registered (operational, informational, named trigger exemption) and measured at apply.
--   3. Issue 1000033 gets a closing probe on its acceptance: the overdue counter reads 0 while both metrics stay registered and on probation, the step exists, and the awaiting metric is measured; and a decision.
--   Issue 2192 (stale metric rows) is not closed by this file: two of its ten stale rows are sample-gated writers (ask_helpful_rate_30d is such a metric, its value 33.3 has not been refreshed since 2026-10-25T08:45Z because
--   qnfo-ai-search writes nothing below 10 ratings) and the other eight have other writers: the owner map is written on its triage row (remediation), because the description of 2192 is rewritten every hour by its
--   producer and would lose it.
-- PREDICTION: after apply metrics_on_probation_overdue stays 0 after 2026-11-18 (the step moves the dates 2 days ahead of them), metrics_awaiting_samples reads 2, the probe of issue 1000033 passes and closes it.
-- spof-review: none added. No DELETE or DROP runs in this file, so it names no BACKUP table beyond the two it creates for the Rollback.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261026_msg1_workflow
-- Rollback: UPDATE fleet_tasks SET definition = json_remove(json_remove(definition, '$.steps[' || (SELECT j.key FROM json_each(fleet_tasks.definition, '$.steps') j WHERE json_extract(j.value, '$.name') = 'awaiting-samples') || ']'), '$.steps[' || (SELECT j.key FROM json_each(fleet_tasks.definition, '$.steps') j WHERE json_extract(j.value, '$.name') = 'probation-sample-gate') || ']'), version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 'metric-refresh' AND instr(definition, '"probation-sample-gate"') > 0 AND instr(definition, '"awaiting-samples"') > 0; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261026_msg1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), last_verdict = (SELECT b.last_verdict FROM bak_20261026_msg1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), verify_probe = (SELECT b.verify_probe FROM bak_20261026_msg1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), action = (SELECT b.action FROM bak_20261026_msg1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), precondition = (SELECT b.precondition FROM bak_20261026_msg1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), module = (SELECT b.module FROM bak_20261026_msg1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), attempts = 0 WHERE class = 'issue-1000033' AND module = 'metric-sample-gate-1'; UPDATE issue_triage SET remediation = substr(remediation, 1, instr(remediation, char(10) || 'OWNERS 2026-10-26 (rem-a2') - 1) WHERE issue_id = 2192 AND instr(COALESCE(remediation, ''), char(10) || 'OWNERS 2026-10-26 (rem-a2') > 0; DELETE FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = 'metrics_awaiting_samples'; DELETE FROM metric_authorship WHERE metric = 'metrics_awaiting_samples';

-- 0. Backups for the Rollback.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_msg1_workflow AS SELECT id, definition, version FROM fleet_tasks WHERE id = 'metric-refresh';

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_msg1_contract AS SELECT class, issue_id, status, last_verdict, verify_probe, action, precondition, module, attempts FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'issue-1000033';

-- 1. The visible count of what cannot measure yet.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO metric_registry (metric, layer, kind, formula, source_of_truth, baseline, target, owner, disposition_actor, refresh_cadence, warning_band, kill_band, last_value, last_refreshed, state, refresh_class) VALUES
  ('metrics_awaiting_samples', 'operational', 'target',
   'COUNT(*) of metric_authorship rows on probation whose metric_registry.last_value IS NULL and whose formula carries a minimum-sample clause (unmeasured below, written once at least, minimum sample): metrics that cannot produce a value until their sample floor is met (METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1, agent_issues 1000033). Counted apart from metrics_on_probation_overdue so a metric that cannot measure yet is neither hidden nor reported as overdue. Trigger exemption: informational, the count falls only when volume arrives (ratings, forecasts), which no lever of the fleet moves; the metrics it lists keep their own triggers',
   'qnfo-audit.metric_authorship + metric_registry, written hourly by fleet_tasks metric-refresh (step awaiting-samples)',
   '2 on 2026-10-26: q08_forecast_void_share and ask_plain_share_7d (ask_helpful_rate_30d is not counted: it has a value, stale since 2026-10-25T08:45Z)',
   'informational (no bound)',
   'qnfo-fleet-control', 'none: reported next to metrics_on_probation_overdue', 'hourly', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNMEASURED', 'computed');

-- 2. The two steps, appended once each (the instr guards make a replay a no-op), and the same statements now.
UPDATE fleet_tasks
SET definition = json_insert(definition, '$.steps[#]', json('{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","name":"probation-sample-gate","sql":"UPDATE metric_authorship SET probation_until = strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''+30 days'') WHERE status = ''probation'' AND probation_until < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''+2 days'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry r WHERE r.metric = metric_authorship.metric AND r.last_value IS NULL AND (instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '''')), ''unmeasured below'') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '''')), ''written once at least'') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '''')), ''minimum sample'') > 0))"}')),
    version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE id = 'metric-refresh' AND instr(definition, '"probation-sample-gate"') = 0;

UPDATE fleet_tasks
SET definition = json_insert(definition, '$.steps[#]', json('{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","name":"awaiting-samples","sql":"UPDATE metric_registry SET last_value = CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_authorship a JOIN metric_registry r ON r.metric = a.metric WHERE a.status = ''probation'' AND r.last_value IS NULL AND (instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '''')), ''unmeasured below'') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '''')), ''written once at least'') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '''')), ''minimum sample'') > 0)) AS TEXT), last_refreshed = strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now''), state = ''MEASURED'' WHERE metric = ''metrics_awaiting_samples''"}')),
    version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE id = 'metric-refresh' AND instr(definition, '"awaiting-samples"') = 0;

UPDATE metric_authorship SET probation_until = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '+30 days') WHERE status = 'probation' AND probation_until < strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '+2 days') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry r WHERE r.metric = metric_authorship.metric AND r.last_value IS NULL AND (instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '')), 'unmeasured below') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '')), 'written once at least') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '')), 'minimum sample') > 0));

UPDATE metric_registry SET last_value = CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_authorship a JOIN metric_registry r ON r.metric = a.metric WHERE a.status = 'probation' AND r.last_value IS NULL AND (instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '')), 'unmeasured below') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '')), 'written once at least') > 0 OR instr(lower(COALESCE(r.formula, '')), 'minimum sample') > 0)) AS TEXT), last_refreshed = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'), state = 'MEASURED' WHERE metric = 'metrics_awaiting_samples';

-- 3. Issue 1000033: a closing probe on its acceptance (it stood on the generic superseded contract), the finding, the decision.
UPDATE remediation_contracts
SET verify_probe = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN CAST(COALESCE((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''metrics_on_probation_overdue''), ''1'') AS REAL) <> 0 THEN ''not met: metrics_on_probation_overdue reads '' || COALESCE((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''metrics_on_probation_overdue''), ''?'') WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_authorship WHERE metric IN (''ask_helpful_rate_30d'', ''q08_forecast_void_share'') AND status = ''probation'') <> 2 THEN ''not met: ask_helpful_rate_30d and q08_forecast_void_share are not both still on probation'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_registry WHERE metric IN (''ask_helpful_rate_30d'', ''q08_forecast_void_share'')) <> 2 THEN ''not met: ask_helpful_rate_30d and q08_forecast_void_share are not both registered'' WHEN instr(COALESCE((SELECT definition FROM fleet_tasks WHERE id = ''metric-refresh''), ''''), ''probation-sample-gate'') = 0 THEN ''not met: the metric-refresh step probation-sample-gate is missing'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''metrics_awaiting_samples'' AND state = ''MEASURED'' AND last_value IS NOT NULL AND last_refreshed >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-180 minutes'')) THEN ''not met: metrics_awaiting_samples is not measured within 180 minutes'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
    verify_transport = 'd1-query', status = 'active', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now'), module = 'metric-sample-gate-1',
    precondition = 'issue 1000033 is open: metrics_on_probation_overdue counts metrics that cannot produce a value below their sample floor',
    action = 'MEASURES the acceptance of the issue: metrics_on_probation_overdue reads 0 while ask_helpful_rate_30d and q08_forecast_void_share stay registered and on probation, the metric-refresh step probation-sample-gate exists (a metric with no sample gate and no value is not touched by it and still counts as overdue), and metrics_awaiting_samples is measured within 180 minutes. METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1'
WHERE class = 'issue-1000033' AND issue_id = 1000033 AND status = 'superseded' AND instr(action, 'VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1') = 1
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = 1000033 AND status = 'open');

UPDATE agent_issues
SET description = description || char(10) || 'FINDING 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1): metrics_on_probation_overdue reads 0 today only because migrations/2026-10-19-impact-per-dollar-zenodo-null.sql moved both probation dates by hand to 2026-11-18T08:02:17Z; the counter lives in the fleet_tick trigger kernel_registries_tick, which is not recreated here (the 04:42Z SQLITE_NOMEM outage of 2026-10-26 came from a fleet_tick trigger). Done by migrations/2026-10-26-metric-sample-gate-1.sql on the data the counter reads: fleet_tasks metric-refresh moves probation_until 30 days ahead for a probation metric with no value and a minimum-sample clause in its formula (a metric with no sample gate and no value still counts as overdue), and the new metric metrics_awaiting_samples keeps them visible, as this issue asks (no dormant marking, no wontfix). Closing probe: contract issue-1000033.'
WHERE id = 1000033 AND status = 'open' AND instr(description, 'FINDING 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1)') = 0;

-- Issue 2192: its description is rewritten every hour by its producer, so the owner map goes on the triage row (remediation), which the producer does not touch.
UPDATE issue_triage
SET remediation = COALESCE(remediation, '') || char(10) || 'OWNERS 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1): the stale rows have four writers, not one defect (read 2026-10-26 18:58Z, last_refreshed against the declared cadence): qnfo-research-exec paper_loop_revisions_24h and papers_awaiting_revision (2026-10-25T08:30:59Z, declared 10m), papers_claim_unaudited and papers_fabricated_claims_open (2026-10-26T04:30:58Z, declared 10m), the pipeline being the one agent_issues 100622 reports stopped by its pace gate; qnfo-gateway seo_crawl_googlebot_7d, seo_crawl_bingbot_7d and seo_indexnow_engines_ok (2026-10-25T09:45:00Z, declared hourly); qnfo-ai-search ask_helpful_rate_30d (2026-10-25T08:45:00Z, declared hourly; its writer gives no value below 10 ratings, the sample-gate family of metrics_awaiting_samples); qnfo-fleet-control breaches_unmapped (2026-10-26T09:12:52Z, declared hourly) and pr_open_over_10m (2026-10-26T18:11:02Z, declared */10). The probe of the contract of this issue counts such rows (a metric never measured is excluded, the producer lists those apart), so the issue closes when each writer refreshes its row; METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1 closes none of them. The metrics never measured are counted by metrics_unmeasured, not by this issue.'
WHERE issue_id = 2192 AND instr(COALESCE(remediation, ''), 'OWNERS 2026-10-26 (rem-a2') = 0
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = 2192 AND status = 'open');

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'rem-a2 (remediation session 2026-10-26)',
  'a metric that cannot produce a value until a sample floor is met should stay visible as awaiting samples and not as overdue, and the rule belongs on the data the counter reads because the counter sits in a fleet_tick trigger that sessions do not recreate',
  'METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1: metric metrics_awaiting_samples registered, steps probation-sample-gate and awaiting-samples appended to fleet_tasks metric-refresh, closing probe and FINDING block on agent_issues 1000033, owner map for the stale rows on the triage row of agent_issues 2192',
  'read 2026-10-26 from live qnfo-audit: metrics_on_probation_overdue 0, ask_helpful_rate_30d and q08_forecast_void_share on probation until 2026-11-18T08:02:17Z (extended by hand on 2026-10-19), 116 probation rows of which 46 have no value and 2 of those carry a minimum-sample clause, kernel_registries_tick counts every probation row past probation_until, the contract of issue 1000033 superseded VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1',
  'applied through the canonical path on merge: metrics_awaiting_samples reads 2 and the probe of issue 1000033 passes',
  'one metric_registry row (one metric_authorship row by trigger), two appended workflow steps (an hourly UPDATE of metric_authorship rows that carry a sample gate and no value, and a count), one contract, one issue description, two backup tables, no trigger, worker, secret or probation row of a metric without a sample gate is touched',
  'the Rollback header of migrations/2026-10-26-metric-sample-gate-1.sql removes both steps by name, restores the contract from bak_20261026_msg1_contract, strips the owner map from the triage row of issue 2192 and deletes the metric and its authorship row (a probation date the step has moved stays where it is)',
  'sample-gated-metric-kept-visible',
  'within 120 minutes of apply: metrics_awaiting_samples reads 2, the probe of issue 1000033 passes and closes it, and metrics_on_probation_overdue still reads 0 after 2026-11-18',
  NULL,
  'node:sqlite replay (migrations/metric-sample-gate-1.test.mjs) with both steps run on fixtures of a gated metric, an ungated metric and a metric with a value, the probe met and unmet, apply_migrations.py --check'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE actor LIKE 'rem-a2%' AND instr(action, 'METRIC-SAMPLE-GATE-1') > 0);
